# Build context of this directory's Dockerfile (docs/ci-fast-deploys/PLAN-2026-09-29.md). BuildKit reads
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile. Keep it the same as apps/web/Dockerfile.dockerignore.
#
# Not a root .dockerignore: Railway's builder (Railpack) applies a root .dockerignore to its own builds too. On
# 2026-09-29 it left apps/api/.release-sha out of the Railway API build (run 36636596664): readiness reported build
# "unknown", the deploy check failed, and the worker, scheduler and web were not shipped.
#
# An allow-list: only what the two images are built from goes to the builder. Everything else stays out — docs/,
# output/, outputs/, obsidian-vault/, apps/factory, services/ — and so does every .env: on a developer machine the root
# .env holds production credentials, and the images are public.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!turbo.json
!patches/
!apps/api/
!apps/web/
!packages/
# The one file outside the workspaces that the web imports (the /design-system catalogue shows VT.1's fixtures).
!docs/fixtures/vt1/fixtures.ts

**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.next
**/.next-*
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
apps/api/.release-sha
